error[ffi_writable_parameter]: `s1` of `strtok` is declared `cstr`, and the header says `char *` — C does not promise to leave it alone
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-writable-parameter.hero:45:5
     |
  45 |     function strtok(s1: cstr, s2: cstr) -> cstr   #~ ffi_writable_parameter
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: §4.20: `s.cstr()` lends the string's own bytes, and they may be shared with other values — a C write through them changes values this program never passed to C, and on a literal it aborts
  note: declare it `ptr` and give `strtok` a buffer C owns, then read the result back
  fix (guess): declare it `ptr`
